  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "title": "Test fixture: a PRESENTATION row whose alias list does not carry its own family's bare name",
  "note": "Rows copied field-for-field from the 19 MB openmrs-ddi-knowledge-base DDInter 2.0 dataset, in KB order, for issue #209. Estrone and Estrone sulfate are two substances the KB files under ONE rxnorm_name (estrone), so the display stem is what keeps them apart; and the third row, Estrone sulfate (topical), is a presentation of the SECOND of them whose aliases carry `estrone` - the FIRST one's display name - and nothing spelled `estrone sulfate`. That is the shape that makes the candidate-set verdict per SUBSTANCE rather than per row: a per-row verdict resolves `estrone` for that presentation, finds it names the other substance, and drops a row of a substance that is in play. The interactions array is empty deliberately - this fixture asserts which rows a name resolves, and no rule of the shipped KB sits on that presentation alone (measured), so a chip-level assertion would have to invent one."
 },
